e alone between D-aminoacylase and L-aminoacylase, obtained by transferring a D-aminoacylase production gene into a host microorganism tolerant to zinc; and a process which comprises culturing the above transformed microorganism in a medium containing zinc ion and obtaining D-aminoacylase from the culture medium at a high efficiency.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un micro-organisme transformé produisant sélectivement de la D-aminoacylase seule entre la D-aminoacylase et la L-aminoacylase, lequel micro-organisme est obtenu par transfert d'un gène de production de D-aminoacylase dans un micro-organisme hôte tolérant le zinc. L'invention concerne également un procédé consistant à cultiver le micro-organisme transformé précité dans un milieu contenant des ions zinc, et à produire de la D-aminoacylase à partir de ce milieu de culture avec un rendement élevé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>